  "notes": "Paper derives new observed constraints on the ALP-proton coupling using Super-Kamiokande (phases I-IV) data via a p -> p gamma from a diffuse galactic SN ALP flux. The excluded region is a closed band: g_ap between ~2e-5 and ~2e-4 for masses 1-70 MeV (95% CL via profiled log-likelihood, Wilks' theorem). Emitted data_points give the LOWER boundary of the exclusion band (~2e-5) spanning 1-70 MeV; the exclusion has an UPPER ceiling at g_ap ~ 2e-4 above which ALPs are trapped in the proto-NS and cannot reach Earth. Numerical values from abstract/text only; exact contour (Fig. 4) not tabulated. Paper also gives a Hyper-Kamiokande projection (~1e-5, ma <= 50 MeV) not included in data_points. Not a DM halo search, so no local DM density assumed. | vector-trace candidate: boundsSK_g_vs_ma_compare.pdf colour (0.79, 0.63, 1.0), 105 pts (selected among 12) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 105))",
